1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,100
The Bible experts knew
where the King would be born.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:04,080
Did they go?

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:08,900
About 700 years before, the prophet Micah
named a small town: Bethlehem.

4
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:11,200
God promised a King from there:

5
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:12,600
“ruler in Israel.”

6
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:14,750
It goes on: “from everlasting.”

7
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:17,800
Bethlehem would be His birthplace,
not His beginning.

8
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:22,500
There, God's promise came true:
Jesus, the King, was born.

9
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,950
Wise men came asking for this King.

10
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:26,850
King Herod asked the experts.

11
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,200
“In Bethlehem of Judaea.”

12
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:31,900
Bethlehem was close by.

13
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:34,500
The Bible never says
the experts went.

14
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:37,900
The wise men went,
and found the child.

15
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,700
Jesus grew up in Galilee.

16
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:42,400
People argued: can the King
come from Galilee?

17
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:45,100
The promise said Bethlehem.
He was born there.

18
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,950
But Jesus came much farther.

19
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,900
He came down from heaven.

20
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:50,600
He died for our sins.

21
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:53,550
On the third day,
He rose from the dead.

22
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,700
Before anyone went to Him,
He came to us.
